      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under GDPR, you must process customer emails and shipping addresses only for specific, lawful purposes like order fulfillment and communicating with the purchaser, ensuring transparency in your privacy policy. You are responsible for keeping this personal data stored securely with limited retention times after the order is completed or the customer requests deletion. Finally, since you handle cross-border physical goods, you must also ensure that your third-party logistics providers in other countries are compliant with EU data protection laws.",
